<item>
<title>Telegram macOS</title>
<description>New:&lt;br&gt;• Hidden chats can be opened from the main mode through a public username, a link or a mention. They open as if you never talked: no earlier messages, media or draft, and what you write there stays visible next time&lt;br&gt;• Hidden chats stay hidden after you log out and log back in on this Mac&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improved:&lt;br&gt;• Hidden channels and groups look like ones you haven't joined; Join brings them back to your main list&lt;br&gt;• Hidden chats no longer show up anywhere else in the main mode: archive, folders, forwarding, Ctrl+Tab, downloads, storage, notification exceptions, export and pickers&lt;br&gt;• Nothing on disk or in the search field shows whether hidden chats are set up&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed:&lt;br&gt;• Closing a chat in hidden mode no longer animates&lt;br&gt;• Oversized icons in "How it works" on non-Retina displays&lt;br&gt;</description>
<pubDate>2026-18-11 11:27:24</pubDate>
